-- title:
--   Local inclusion and separable residue extension over the Gauss ring
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, $M'\ge 1$ an integer with $q\nmid M'$, and $L$ a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$, together with a ring embedding $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb C$ sending $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((X))$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion function field over $\mathbb Q$ of $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$, where $H=\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$; that field is generated by the ratios $f/g$ of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for the relevant group. Let $K_0$ be the analogous base change of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_0(M')$, assumed contained in $K$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$. Let $W_0\subseteq K$ and $O_0\subseteq K_0$ be the valuation subrings consisting of those $f$ for which $f\cdot y=x$ for some $x,y\in A[[X]]$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Then for every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ fixing $K_0$ pointwise, writing $B=\tau^{-1}(W_0)$ for the pullback valuation subring: an element of $K_0$ lies in $B$ exactly when it lies in $O_0$; and, with respect to the resulting $O_0$-algebra structure on $B$, the map $O_0\to B$ is a local homomorphism and the residue field extension $\mathrm{ResidueField}(O_0)\to\mathrm{ResidueField}(B)$ is separable.
--
--   The statement records the local behaviour of the Gauss (cuspidal) valuation on the function field of the full-level modular curve $X_H(q^2M')$ over the corresponding valuation of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-floor, in the form needed for an Igusa-type analysis of the fibre at $q$: the two valuations are compatible, and the residue extension at the cusp is separable. It is used in the proof of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_comap_eq_and_ramificationIdx_eq_one_and_isSeparable_of_over_gauss_gamma0_mul_xH`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_comap_eq_and_ramificationIdx_eq_one_and_isSeparable_of_over_gauss_gamma0_mul_xH), where it supplies the clause asserting local inclusion with unramified, separable residue data.
